# The K3.1 prompt pass on the split dial's arena (expert_nvme_tier_for_passes) against the re-cut's floor arena. One K3.1
# request at bp on the arenapass tree's bloomery-serve, the defaults (the pass), D=512, 512 generated, ctx 2048, 232G, two drives.
kind: calibration
question: does the pass's load decode at the step's rate once its plan keeps the dial's arena, and what does the prompt pass read then
term: decode tok/s @ D=512, n_predict 512, one cold request, --place bp, --ctx-size 2048, BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=232G, the tree's bloomery-serve
unit: tok/s
predict: 4.5..5.3
condition: tools/ref/k31-nvme-probe.sh with K31_PROBE_SERVE the arenapass tree's target/release/bloomery-serve, K31_PROBE_D=512,
  K31_PROBE_N=512, K31_PROBE_ENV="BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=232G", the two-drive sidecar in place; the plan line beside it
reason: [derived] the step's plan at 232G (arena 228.8 GB, 374 slots) decoded 4.99 under --prefill steps and the pass's floor
  plan (arena 22.6 GB, 37 slots) 2.94 (k31-rel-serve.card outcome 2026-11-08). The pass's plan now takes the dial's arena; its
  card holds the pass's reserve beside the experts (card_experts 1852 against the step's 1947 at 2048), about 5 % fewer card
  experts [derived from the two plan lines], so the decode is the step's within the cold request's scatter.
  The prompt rate is read, not predicted: the floor plan read 212 GB of host share through the mapping and 297 GB paged a pass;
  this plan pages ~500 GB through the arena (O_DIRECT, two drives), most ids landing in the 374-slot arena after the first
  pass.
decide-in: the next K3.1 seat default and the README's pass/steps limit (gone when decode is in band and the prompt holds ≥ 8)
decide-below: under 4.5: read the plan line's arena and the nvtier record (copies=, slots) before suspecting the step
decide-above: above 5.3: read the witness block and the plan line before crediting
# outcome 2026-11-08 on arenapass 5a71362da (the tree's target/release/bloomery-serve, built in ~/repo/bloomery-k31main-narrow-head),
#  one cold request, D=512, 512 generated, ctx 2048, 232G, two drives: tg 4.46 / pp 10.22, load 66 s; the plan arena=228534329344
#  (374 slots) where the floor plan read 22.6 GB; listening prompt=pass; nvtier copies=2, misses 51,759, fill_bytes 342.1 GB,
#  evictions 18,031. 0.04 under the band: decide-below read the arena (the dial's) and copies (2), so the gap to the steps load's
#  4.99 is the pass's card reserve (card_experts 1885 against 1947) and the prompt union's churn in the arena, not the step.
#  decide-in: the pass stays the default (165 s for 512 + 512 against 215 s on the floor arena and 237 s stepped); README's limit
#  names steps as the pick past a reply of about 7 times the prompt [derived].
